Package: paramounter
Title: Measure LC-MS Processing Parameters Directly from Your Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("William", "Oldham", , "wm.oldham@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3029-4866")),
    person("Jian", "Guo", role = "cph"),
    person("Tao", "Huan", role = "cph")
  )
Description: Measures universal liquid chromatography-mass spectrometry
    parameters - mass tolerance, noise level, peak width, signal-to-noise
    ratio, peak height, and instrument mass and retention time shift -
    directly from centroided data files, then translates them into
    processing settings for 'xcms', MS-DIAL, and MZmine. Unlike approaches
    that search a parameter space against an objective function, the
    parameters are measured from the data itself, so a single pass over the
    files is enough. Implements the method of Guo and Huan (2022)
    <doi:10.1021/acs.analchem.1c04758>.
